── one element: the case a `len < 2` guard and a `len == 0` guard differ on ──
fsum(one)          4612811918334230528
fmean(one)         4612811918334230528
fvariance(one)     -2251799813685248
  and the values themselves, so the bits above can be read:
    fsum(one)      2.50000000000000000e+00
    fmean(one)     2.50000000000000000e+00
    fvariance(two) 5.00000000000000000e-01
── a single-element array is a sum of itself, and its mean is itself ──
  fsum(one)  == 2.5   true
  fmean(one) == 2.5   true
  fsum(two)  == 6.0   true
  fmean(two) == 3.0   true
── the NaN these produce carries its sign bit, and it does not matter ──
  math.nan          nan
  its bits          -2251799813685248
  fmean(empty)      nan
  0.0 / 0.0         nan
  all three the same NaN: true
  and the sign never escapes: 1/nan is a NaN, not an infinity: true
── in place, where there is no sum to get wrong ──
  after fscale and faxpy: 23.000000 46.000000
  and both on an empty pair leave it empty: 0
